# Whitelist build context. The cvmfs demo build (deploy/cvmfs/docker/Dockerfile)
# needs only ./config + ./src + its deploy files. The k8s-tests images
# (images/authority, images/test-runner, images/server, images/client-fuse) also
# need ./tests + ./utils, and the server module build needs ./config + ./src.
# The RPM builder Dockerfiles need ./packaging (spec file), ./client (tools),
# ./contrib + ./docs (%doc payload), and the top-level LICENSE/README/pytest
# files the spec installs — plus the whole ./deploy/cvmfs tree, since the spec's
# %install runs `make -C client install-automount`, which pulls mount.cvmfs,
# auto.cvmfs and etc/cvmfs/** from there (not just the demo docker/ subdir).
# Everything else (.git, .rpmbuild, node_modules, scratch) stays out.
*
!config
!src
!shared
!client
!packaging
!contrib
!docs
!LICENSE
!README.md
!conftest.py
!pytest.ini
!requirements.txt
!deploy/cvmfs
!deploy/fail2ban
!deploy/docker
!deploy/compose
!tests
!utils
!k8s-tests
# Keep the context lean — never ship caches, scratch, generated doxygen output,
# or vendored chart archives.
docs/doxygen
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
tests/.pytest_cache
tests/.tmp
k8s-tests/charts/**/charts
k8s-tests/charts/**/Chart.lock

# Host build output stays out. Every image here compiles from source (`COPY . .`
# or `COPY client ...`, then make), and Docker preserves mtimes, so an artifact
# carried in from the developer's machine can look up to date and be reused
# instead of rebuilt. Two ways that bites, both reachable today because only the
# RPM spec runs `make -C client clean` first -- deploy/docker and the k8s server
# image do not:
#   - a .d dependency file names the HOST's header paths (a macOS build writes
#     /usr/local/Cellar/krb5/.../krb5.h), and the client Makefile's
#     `-include $(DEPS)` then dies with "No rule to make target" on a path no
#     container has;
#   - a stale .o/.a is linked rather than recompiled: Mach-O inputs fail the
#     link outright, and a Linux host's leftovers build silently wrong.
# Excluding client/bin also keeps the spec's `test -x client/bin/<tool>`
# assertion honest -- it must prove what the CONTAINER built, not what the
# developer happened to have lying around.
**/*.o
**/*.a
**/*.so
**/*.so.*
**/*.dylib
**/*.dSYM
client/bin
# Dependency files, scoped to the three trees that compile: a bare `**/*.d`
# would also match DIRECTORIES named *.d, and the fail2ban filter.d / jail.d
# and CVMFS default.d, domain.d, config.d trees the RPM spec installs are
# exactly that shape (the same trap .gitignore's `!*.d/` exists for).
client/**/*.d
shared/**/*.d
src/**/*.d

# AppleDouble sidecars a macOS host leaves beside files (see .gitignore).
**/._*
